; every expression tree flattens to a NON-EMPTY leaf list: 0 < len(flatten e).
; Composed, no induction: 0 < count e [count-positive] and count e = len(flatten e) [count-flatten], so rewriting count into len(flatten) gives 0 < len(flatten e). A non-emptiness invariant on the LOWERED form -- the lowering of a (necessarily non-empty) tree never produces the empty list, the kind of fact a verifier carries across a structural transform.
